.TH ANTIGRAVITY\-UPDATE 1 "2026" "antigravity-update @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
antigravity\-update \- install or update Antigravity IDE, wherever it lives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B antigravity\-update
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds an existing Antigravity IDE installation and updates it in place, then
refreshes its desktop integration.
.PP
The install directory is discovered rather than assumed, in this order: the
\fBantigravity\fR or \fBantigravity\-ide\fR launcher on your \fBPATH\fR,
followed up to the directory that actually contains
\fBresources/app/product.json\fR; the \fBExec=\fR line of an installed
desktop entry; and finally the usual prefixes \(em \fB/usr/share\fR,
\fB/usr/local/share\fR, \fB/opt\fR and
\fB~/.local/share\fR.
.PP
If nothing is installed, you are told so and asked whether to install it and
where. With
.B \-\-yes
it installs to the default location without asking.
.PP
Compares the installed version with the newest published on
\fBantigravity.google\fR. If the site is ahead, the new build is downloaded,
verified and rsynced into place.
.PP
The download is resumable, so an interrupted run can simply be repeated. Before
the archive is trusted its size is checked against what the server reported and
its table of contents is listed, because a truncated resumable download
otherwise looks like a success.
.PP
.B sudo
is used only when the install directory really is not yours to write, so an
installation under your home directory needs no password at all. Files the IDE
writes itself are preserved across the update, and the Chromium sandbox is
restored to setuid root, without which the IDE refuses to start.
.SS Desktop integration
After installing, the desktop entry, the icon and the command\-line launchers
are rebuilt, so the application appears properly in the activities overview
instead of as a nameless generic window. The icon is taken from the one the
application ships in \fBresources/app/resources/linux\fR and installed into
the hicolor theme, with a copy in \fB/usr/share/pixmaps\fR for desktops that
ignore hicolor.
.PP
A system\-wide install writes to \fB/usr/share/applications\fR and
\fB/usr/local/bin\fR; an install under your home directory writes to
\fB~/.local/share/applications\fR and \fB~/.local/bin\fR instead.
.PP
Use
.B \-\-desktop
to rebuild just that, without touching the installation \(em handy when a
launcher has gone missing or is showing the wrong icon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Report the installed and available versions, then exit without changing
anything. Exits \fB3\fR when an update is available, which makes it easy to
drive from a script.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Do everything except the install itself: resolve, download, verify, extract.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Reinstall even when the installed version is already current.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep the downloaded archive instead of deleting it once the install succeeds.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Use this install directory instead of discovering one.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask anything. If nothing is installed, install to the default location.
.TP
.B \-\-desktop
Only rebuild the desktop entry, the icon and the launchers, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-desktop
Update the files but leave desktop integration alone.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Already up to date, or updated successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Something went wrong.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, or a required program is missing.
.TP
.B 3
With
.BR \-\-check :
an update is available.
.TP
.B 4
With
.BR \-\-check :
Antigravity IDE is not installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANTIGRAVITY_INSTALL_DIR
Same as
.BR \-\-dir .
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask whether an update exists, without installing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
antigravity\-update \-\-check
.EE
.RE
.PP
Only act when there is something to do:
.PP
.RS
.EX
antigravity\-update \-\-check || antigravity\-update
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install for the first time, unattended, into your home directory:
.PP
.RS
.EX
antigravity\-update \-\-yes \-\-dir ~/.local/share/antigravity\-ide
.EE
.RE
.PP
The launcher lost its icon:
.PP
.RS
.EX
antigravity\-update \-\-desktop
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update\-every\-thing (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @MAINTAINER@.
